# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
venv/
*.egg-info/

# OS
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Editor
.vscode/
.idea/

# Local secrets — NEVER commit
.env
.env.local
*.token
*.pem

# Engineering binary artifacts
#
# Policy: small artifacts (<~1 MB STEPs, snapshot PNGs, BOM CSVs)
# live in `artifacts/<discipline>/` directly. Larger ones (full CAD
# assemblies, dense FEA result files, full PCB Gerbers in zip) should
# be referenced by an artifact manifest pointing to git-LFS or an
# external vault — see dev-docs/architecture/artifact-manifest.md.
#
# If your project needs a stricter "no binaries in repo" policy,
# uncomment the patterns below in YOUR project's .gitignore.
#
# *.step
# *.STEP
# *.prt
# *.PRT
# *.iges
# *.IGES
# *.sldprt
# *.sldasm
# *.slddrw
# *.f3d
# *.f3z

# Always ignore: editor backups and intermediate sim blobs
*.kicad_pcb-bak
*.kicad_sch-bak
*.PcbDoc.bak
*.SchDoc.bak
*.raw
*.simulation

# Atopile build outputs (regenerable from .ato sources)
electrical/*/build/
electrical/*/*/build/
electrical/*/logs/
electrical/*/*/logs/

# Atopile writes timestamped backups of the layout + pcbnew session
# state on every build:
#   <output_base>.<YYYYMMDD>-<HHMMSS>.kicad_pcb  ← pre-build PCB snapshot
#   <output_base>.<YYYYMMDD>-<HHMMSS>.kicad_prl  ← pcbnew session state
# These are build-trail noise, not deliverables. The real fab-ready PCB
# gets promoted from `layouts/<target>/<target>.kicad_pcb` to
# `artifacts/electrical/<board>-<rev>.kicad_pcb` by each board's
# `export.py`. Ignore the stubs.
artifacts/electrical/*.????????-??????.kicad_pcb
artifacts/electrical/*.????????-??????.kicad_prl
